to him, I know that he shall rise again in the resurrection at the last day.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙzJesus said unto her, I am the resurrection, and the life: he that believeth in me, though he were dead, yet shall he live:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙNand whosoever liveth and believeth in me shall never die. Believest thou this?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙtShe saith unto him, Yea, Lord: I believe that thou art the Christ, the Son of God, which should come into the world.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse%¦versesš„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‚And when she had so said, she went her way, and called Mary her sister secretly, saying, The Master is come, and calleth for thee.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ@As soon as she heard that, she arose quickly, and came unto him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙUNow Jesus was not yet come into the town, but was in that place where Martha met him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ»The Jews then which were with her in the house, and comforted her, when they saw Mary, that she rose up hastily and went out, followed her, saying, She goeth unto the grave to weep there.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ™Then when Mary was come where Jesus was, and saw him, she fell down at his feet, saying unto him, Lord, if thou hadst been here, my brother had not died.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ€When Jesus therefore saw her weeping, and the Jews also weeping which came with her, he groaned in the spirit, and was troubled,¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙIand said, Where have ye laid him? They said unto him, Lord, come and see.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤text«Jesus wept.¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ,Then said the Jews, Behold how he loved him!¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙƒAnd some of them said, Could not this man, which opened the eyes of the blind, have caused that even this man should not have died?¦layout ªlast_verse%…¤book*§chapter«first_verse&ªlast_verse,¦verses—„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙfJesus therefore again groaning in himself cometh to the grave. It was a cave, and a stone lay upon it.¦layout ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙJesus said, Take ye away the stone. Martha, the sister of him that was dead, saith unto him, Lord, by this time he stinketh: for he hath been dead four days.¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙpJesus saith unto her, Said I not unto thee, that, if thou wouldest believe, thou shouldest see the glory of God?¦layout ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ›Then they took away the stone from the place where the dead was laid. And Jesus lifted up his eyes, and said, Father, I thank thee that thou hast heard me.¦layout ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‰And I knew that thou hearest me always: but because of the people which stand by I said it, that they may believe that thou hast sent me.¦layout ªlast_verse*„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙMAnd when he thus had spoken, he cried with a loud voice, Lazarus, come forth.¦layout ªlast_verse+„¥verse,¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¥And he that was dead came forth, bound hand and foot with graveclothes: and his face was bound about with a napkin. Jesus saith unto them, Loose him, and let him go.¦layout ªlast_verse,…¤book*§chapter«first_verse-ªlast_verse5¦verses™„¥verse-¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙcThen many of the Jews which came to Mary, and had seen the things which Jesus did, believed on him.¦layout ªlast_verse-„¥verse.¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ\But some of them went their ways to the Pharisees, and told them what things Jesus had done.¦layout ªlast_verse.„¥verse/¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙtThen gathered the chief priests and the Pharisees a council, and said, What do we? for this man doeth many miracles.¦layout ªlast_verse/„¥verse0¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyIf we let him thus alone, all men will believe on him: and the Romans shall come and take away both our place and nation.¦layout ªlast_verse0„¥verse1¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙnAnd one of them, named Caiaphas, being the high priest that same year, said unto them, Ye know nothing at all,¦layout ªlast_verse1„¥verse2¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙwnor consider that it is expedient for us, that one man should die for the people, and that the whole nation perish not.¦layout ªlast_verse2„¥verse3¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙwAnd this spake he not of himself: but being high priest that year, he prophesied that Jesus should die for that nation;¦layout ªlast_verse3„¥verse4¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ|and not for that nation only, but that also he should gather together in one the children of God that were scattered abroad.¦layout ªlast_verse4„¥verse5¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙLThen from that day forth they took counsel together for to put him to death.¦layout ªlast_verse5…¤book*§chapter«first_verse6ªlast_verse9¦verses”„¥verse6¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ°Jesus therefore walked no more openly among the Jews; but went thence unto a country near to the wilderness, into a city called Ephraim, and there continued with his disciples.¦layout ªlast_verse6„¥verse7¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ„And the Jews' passover was nigh at hand: and many went out of the country up to Jerusalem before the passover, to purify themselves.¦layout ªlast_verse7„¥verse8¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‡Then sought they for Jesus, and spake among themselves, as they stood in the temple, What think ye, that he will not come to the feast?¦layout ªlast_verse8„¥verse9¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ—Now both the chief priests and the Pharisees had given a commandment, that, if any man knew where he were, he should shew it, that they might take him.¦layout ªlast_verse9